              <li><strong>Zero Dietary Restrictions:</strong> Enjoy apples, popcorn, nuts, and crisp snacks without worrying about dislodging brackets.</li>
              <li><strong>Superior Gum Hygiene:</strong> Brush and floss normally without threading needles or maneuvering around wires, minimizing plaque buildup.</li>
              <li><strong>Fewer Clinic Visits:</strong> Receive multiple sequential sets in advance, requiring brief progress reviews every 6 to 8 weeks.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-sand/40 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-3">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-japandi-clay"></span>
              <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Traditional Metal &amp; Ceramic Braces</h4>
            </div>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside leading-relaxed">
              <li><strong>Conspicuous Metal Look:</strong> Dark brackets and metallic archwires dominate your smile for 18 to 36 months.</li>
              <li><strong>Permanently Glued:</strong> Fixed to tooth enamel throughout treatment; cannot be removed for events or photos.</li>
              <li><strong>Severe Dietary Bans:</strong> Hard, crunchy, or sticky foods must be strictly avoided to prevent broken brackets.</li>
              <li><strong>Difficult Oral Cleaning:</strong> Food traps easily around brackets and wires, drastically increasing the risk of enamel white spots and gingivitis.</li>
              <li><strong>Frequent Emergency Appointments:</strong> Requires monthly manual wire tightenings, emergency wax applications, and repairs.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Clinical Conditions Treated with Aligners -->
