      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Daily Wear &amp; Maintenance: How to Care for Your Aligners
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Maintaining pristine clear aligners requires simple daily habits that keep them invisible and odor-free:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Gentle Lukewarm Rinsing</span>
            <p>Rinse your aligners with lukewarm water every time you take them out. Never use boiling or hot water, as elevated temperatures can warp the precision polymer matrix.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Soft-Bristle Toothbrushing</span>
            <p>Brush your aligners gently using a soft-bristled brush and clear antibacterial soap or specialized aligner cleaning crystals. Avoid abrasive toothpastes that scratch the clear surface.</p>
          </div>
